    }
  ],
  "summary": "The claim 'Avoid drinking coffee on an empty stomach to prevent acidity' lacks direct evidence from the provided studies. D1 indicates coffee promotes gastro-oesophageal reflux but not dyspepsia, while D2 shows coffee may affect gastroduodenal mucosa permeability. Neither study addresses acidity prevention through avoiding coffee on empty stomach. The claim's recommendation is not tested in the studies, and the causal relationship implied is not supported by the data. The evidence strength is limited due to indirect findings and lack of direct measurement of acidity prevention in the context of the claim's recommendation.",
